seg-e732ac99a9ae = Exact parity-subspace split of a measurement error into the part RAIM cannot see and the part it can. For the linearised snapshot model y = G·x + e, any error dy decomposes uniquely into a BLIND component in range(G) — absorbed as a state error S·dy and annihilated by the residual projector Pperp = I − G·S, so invisible to ANY residual test, not merely to a particular threshold — and a DETECTABLE component in parity space. The module returns the projector, the split, and the blind fraction, so a caller can quantify how much of a specific error a snapshot monitor is structurally unable to report. Applied to the real inter-ephemeris floor: the metre-level DE440-vs-INPOP21a and DE440-vs-EPM2021 disagreement in the geocentric Moon position is absorbed almost entirely as user position error (median blind fraction { "1.000000" }; median blind position error { "2.3955" } m and { "2.0050" } m) against a parity residual at the { "1e-15" } m level

